four cycles are considered as a training set, and the next four cycles are picked for testing the networks. At the second test case for the cylinder, free-stream velocity U∞ is decreased relative to the time from its value corresponding to Re = 3900 as U∞ = U∞,Re=3900/t, where t is the time. The simulation time step is 0.2, and snapshots are collected from the velocity field at every ten time steps. 332 snapshots are extracted from the wake of the cylinder, and 166 snapshots are used as the training set. Variation of lift coefficient besides training and testing data sets are shown in Fig. 2. The gradual decrease of the free-stream velocity weakens the vortex shedding and leads to the change in its frequency. Reynolds number varies from 3355 to 676, as it is depicted in Fig. 3. For the oscillating airfoil test case, the flow around a pitch oscillating NACA0012 airfoil is simulated at Reynolds number Re = U∞C/ν of 1.35 × 105, where C is the airfoil chord. Airfoil oscillates sinusoidally (α = αmean + αamp × sin(Ωt)) about its 1
