Long short-term memory (LSTM) was proposed by Hochreiter and Schmidhuber in 1997 [63]. LSTM is an artificial recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture designed for learning of the sequential data such as numerical or experimental time series and to overcome the forgetting problem in conventional RNNs [64]. An LSTM neural network unit is comprised of an input gate, a cell
