D. Hyperparameter Analysis
The number of layers and the number of neurons in the hidden layers of both autoencoder and LSTM networks besides their activation functions are the hyperparameters of the presented method. An analysis of the hyperparameters is conducted, and the results for the most important ones are presented in Fig. 8 for the cylinder test 2. Here, the performance of the autoencoder and LSTM networks in reconstruction and prediction of the testing data is investigated using three different activation functions, i.e., tanh, ReLU, and softplus, three different number of hidden layers for the autoencoder network (1, 2, 3), and three different number of LSTM cells (10, 100, 600) in the LSTM network. 15% of the train data set is considered as the validation set. Results are presented as the validation loss during the training process and R2 value of the prediction or reconstruction of the testing data. Note that error for the autoencoder network is the error in reconstruction of the flow-field from


